# Repos a reviewer of THIS repo may search and cite, materialized under
# .siblings/<owner>/<repo>. Declared rather than left to the fallback so
# the set is the one this repo actually depends on.
#
# One per line. The reviewer host must also carry a SOURCE_PATHS entry for
# each, or the sibling reports as `missing` and is never searched.
#
# `plow` owns every owner-set chat fact this plugin reads or writes -- the
# grant, the roster, `trusted`, contact labels. `plow-hermes-agent` bakes this
# tree into the image and pins it; `agent-mgr` pins and installs it by SHA for
# the Docker fleet. Both decide where these files land, so a change to the
# installed set has to be read against them. `latch` owns the gog grammar and
# the tool copy this plugin's latch guidance (LATCH_PROMPT) restates.

plow-pbc/plow
plow-pbc/plow-hermes-agent
plow-pbc/agent-mgr
plow-pbc/latch

# Upstream. `plow_chat` is a Hermes platform adapter — it subclasses
# `BasePlatformAdapter` and is the only repo here that imports upstream
# Python symbols — so "did Hermes already solve this?" is a real review
# question and the four entries above cannot answer it. Both are SUBTREES
# of an operator-staged mirror: the framework is ~2M LOC and only its peer
# set belongs in the corpus.
#
#   hermes-gateway-platforms — the base class plus ADDING_A_PLATFORM.md,
#     which enumerates what the plugin system already handles (adapter
#     creation, config parsing, user authorization, cron delivery,
#     send_message routing, system-prompt hints, status display).
#   hermes-platform-adapters — the framework's own ~22 adapters. They are
#     worked examples of the same extension points this repo touches;
#     bluebubbles is the closest peer (PROVIDER = "imessage").
#
# Upstream mirrors are forks and org-sync excludes forks, so these are
# operator-staged and not auto-refreshed. If they report `missing`, the
# mirror is absent on this host — that is a coverage gap, not a clean run.

NousResearch/hermes-gateway-platforms
NousResearch/hermes-platform-adapters
